# Clipboard Viewer with text Notepad copied: the viewer's keys of arch311-ref/scn/clipbrd-note.scn
# Notepad (note-np.txt, run first headless on the same drive and clipboard) opens SYSTEM\CBNOTE.TXT,
# selects all, copies and exits; the viewer then shows the text (as Auto, OEM Text, Text), saves NOTE.CLP
# and clears the clipboard. Real 3.11: arch311-ref/scn/clipbrd-note.scn (Program Manager the shell,
# run=clipbrd.exe notepad.exe), so its frames are compared inside the viewer's window (and the box).
# regress: CLIPBRD_NOTEPAD=apps/clipbrd/tests/note-np.txt sh apps/clipbrd/tests/run.sh "$TEST" "$OUT"
# compare: clipbrd-note/04.png 01.png 0 0 324 240
# compare: clipbrd-note/05.png 02.png 0 0 324 240
# compare: clipbrd-note/06.png 03.png 0 0 324 240
# compare: clipbrd-note/07.png 04.png 0 0 324 240
# compare: clipbrd-note/10.png 06.png 0 0 324 240
# compare: clipbrd-note/11.png 07.png active ignore 320 240 333 261
# compare: clipbrd-note/12.png 08.png 0 0 324 240
# file: files/note.clp run-clipbrd-note/WINDOWS/NOTE.CLP apps/clipbrd/tests/clpcmp.py
sleep 400
sleep 400
shot shots/01.png
key alt
key d
sleep 400
shot shots/02.png
key esc
key esc
key alt
key d
key o
sleep 400
shot shots/03.png
key alt
key d
key t
sleep 400
shot shots/04.png
key alt
key f
key a
sleep 400
shot shots/05.png
key n
key o
key t
key e
key period
key c
key l
key p
key enter
sleep 400
shot shots/06.png
key alt
key e
key d
sleep 400
shot shots/07.png
key y
sleep 400
shot shots/08.png
quit
